    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d459">

                <pb facs="1155" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1943/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">
                    J.C.S. Files</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the British Chiefs of Staff</hi><anchor
                        n="1" xml:id="d459-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        C.C.S. 246/1</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Quebec</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-08-21">21 August 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Movement of the “Queens”</hi><anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d459-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>At the 94th Meeting of the Combined Chiefs of Staff during the 
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Trident</hi>
                     Conference,<anchor n="3" xml:id="d459-f3"/> approval was given to the
                        “<hi rendition="#italic">Queens</hi>” running on <pb facs="1156" n="1042"
                        xml:id="pg1042"/> a 28 day cycle as at that time the urgency of lifting
                    personnel was not as great as it is now.</p>
                <p>It is understood that a situation is developing in which it is essential to lift
                    as many personnel as possible, and in view of the longer nights we recommend
                    that the Combined Chiefs of Staff should now approve that the “<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Queens</hi>” should revert to running on a 21 day
                    cycle.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d459-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d459-f1-content">
                <p>For the action taken on this paper at the 115th Meeting of the Combined Chiefs of
                    Staff, August 23, 1943, see <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref
                        target="#pg939">p. 939</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d459-f2" n="2" xml:id="d459-f2-content">
                <p>i.e., the requisitioned passenger liners <hi rendition="#italic">Queen
                        Elizabeth</hi> and <hi rendition="#italic">Queen Mary.</hi>
                </p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d459-f3" n="3" xml:id="d459-f3-content">
                <p>See <hi rendition="#italic">ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg179">p. 179</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
